We outline the proof of the geometric Langlands conjecture.

It is well known.
It is well known.
It is well known.
It is well known.
It is well known.

Suppose 800.

The proof is 800 pages. We push them onto the stack.
The pages are there. The stack holds them.

Clearly they are correct.
Clearly the details can be checked.

It is well known that the proof has been announced.
It is well known that the proof has been submitted.
It is well known that the proof is being refereed.

Publish.

The 800 pages have been popped.
They went to the Annals. Or they went nowhere.
The distinction is not observable from outside
the editorial board.

QED.
